   464	Fix $N\ge2$, a total order on $S$, and for each $w\in W$ a reduced Coxeter word $\rho(w)$,
   465	with $\rho(1)=\epsilon$. For definiteness choose the lex-least reduced Coxeter word: repeatedly
   466	remove the least left descent. This is a computation in the finite group $W$, not an
   467	Artin-group normal-form oracle. The positive lift of $w$ is independent of the chosen
   468	reduced word by Matsumoto's theorem. For simples $u,v$, use the finite weak-order join to define
   469	$u\backslash v=u^{-1}(u\vee v)\in W$; its positive lift is the right complement in (1.1).
