     1	"""Exact finite automata for the normal forms and for the leading words of the
     2	reduced deg-lex Groebner-Shirshov basis of a finite-type Artin group in the
     3	Artin-Garside generators (positive part), built directly from W.
     4	
     5	Theory (proof.md, Lemmas 3-4): a positive word v_1..v_L is a normal form
     6	(deg-lex-smallest representative, not divisible by Delta) iff for every k
     7	  (L) for all t < v_k with m(t,v_k) < oo:  Pi(t,v_k) does not left-divide [v_{k+1}..v_L],
     8	      where Pi(t,v_k) = v_k\\t is the alternating word t v_k t ... of length m(t,v_k)-1;
     9	  (D) v_k^{-1} Delta does not left-divide [v_{k+1}..v_L].
    10	Reading left to right we keep the antichain of pending 'obligations' (simple
    11	elements that must not divide the rest); reading y maps c -> y\\c (right
    12	complement) and the word dies when some obligation becomes 1.
    13	
    14	Minimal reducible words (= leading words of the reduced GS basis restricted to
    15	positive words) are u with u[:-1], u[1:] normal and u not normal; they are
    16	counted with a pair automaton (full run, run started at the second letter).
    17	
    18	Usage: python3 work/automaton.py TYPE n [--m M] [--order 0,2,1] [--L 60] [--monoid]
